<title>UK: TABLE-Sketchley sees yr loss, but sales up.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Sketchley sees yr loss, but sales up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) (loss)	 5.0		  vs   4.7</p>
<p> Final Dividend (pence)   nil		  vs   2.4</p>
<p> Pre-tax loss		 4.3		  vs   3.5</p>
<p> Turnover		   157.6		  vs 139.1</p>
<p>NOTE - Earnings per share before exceptional charge nil versus 4.9 pence. An exceptional charge of 5.1 million stg was made, reflecting additional costs involved in reorganising the retail division. Also, an adjustment of 4.8 million was charged at the operating level within the retail unit following a number of accounting errors discovered in May. The company had paid an interim dividend of 1.1 pence, unchanged from the previous year.</p>
<p>Full name of dry cleaning company - Sketchley Plc.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
</text>
